# Spam Message Detection

A text-classification project that compares Multinomial Naive Bayes and Linear SVM for separating spam from legitimate (`ham`) messages. The pipeline tokenizes and stems text, removes English stop words, and converts messages to TF-IDF features.

> **Dataset note:** The default UCI corpus contains SMS messages, not email. For email-specific filtering, train on a representative, labeled email dataset. This project is educational and does not guarantee phishing detection.

## Features

- Downloads the UCI SMS Spam Collection by default.
- Supports a local CSV with `label` and `message` columns.
- Applies tokenization, stop-word removal, stemming, and TF-IDF.
- Evaluates Naive Bayes and Linear SVM with accuracy, per-class precision/recall, and a confusion matrix.
- Saves trained models for classifying new messages.

## Project structure

```text
spam-detection/
├── requirements.txt
├── src/
│   ├── train_model.py
│   └── predict.py
└── outputs/                 # created by training
```

## Setup and run

```bash
py -m venv .venv
# Windows PowerShell:
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
# macOS/Linux:
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python src/train_model.py
```

Classify a message:

```bash
python src/predict.py --text "Claim your free prize now!"
python src/predict.py --text "Are we still meeting today?" --model "Naive Bayes"
```

Train with your own labeled dataset:

```bash
python src/train_model.py --data path/to/messages.csv
```

The training command saves models to `outputs/spam_models.joblib`. Review messages before acting on a model's classification; false positives and missed spam are possible.

## Dataset and references

- [UCI SMS Spam Collection](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/228/sms)
- [scikit-learn text feature extraction](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/feature_extraction.html#text-feature-extraction)
